# Normalize line endings in the REPO so the home and work machines (both
# Windows 11) can't disagree and produce phantom "everything changed" diffs.
# `* text=auto` stores all text as LF in git; Windows still checks out CRLF
# locally, but git compares against the normalized blob, so no churn. (Exception:
# the generated dist/ bundles below are pinned byte-for-byte -- see that note.)
* text=auto

# Explicit text types (belt and suspenders)
*.py    text
*.md    text
*.txt   text
*.json  text
*.html  text
*.css   text
*.js    text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.cfg   text
*.ini   text
*.toml  text

# Platform-native scripts keep their expected endings
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Vendored third-party JS (loom/vendor/) -- byte-for-byte as downloaded, never
# line-ending-normalized (overrides the `*.js text` rule above; more specific wins).
loom/vendor/*.js binary

# Committed build artifacts in the dist/ dirs are GENERATED (vite/esbuild output), not
# hand-edited source: the bundlers emit LF, a Windows checkout's core.autocrlf=true wants CRLF
# for `text` files, and that mismatch leaves them PERMANENTLY "modified" with an EMPTY diff that
# no `git add` can ever clear (two weeks of phantom churn on loom/dist/master-storyboard.bundle.css,
# and the same latent trap on gallery/dist/app.css|app.js). Mark them byte-for-byte so git never
# EOL-normalizes generated output -- same rule, same reason as loom/vendor above. The blobs are
# already LF; this only stops the CRLF round-trip. More specific than the `*.css`/`*.js text` rules
# above, so it wins for these paths.
gallery/dist/*.css   -text
gallery/dist/*.js    -text
gallery/dist/*.html  -text
gallery/dist/*.json  -text
loom/dist/*.css      -text
loom/dist/*.js       -text

# Binary — git must never touch these
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
